WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.267
-I'm so happy to see you.

00:00:02.267 --> 00:00:04.167
Welcome back, and thank you
for being Goatleg Greg.

00:00:04.167 --> 00:00:05.267
I appreciate it.
-You know, I've

00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:06.801
got goatskin trousers.

00:00:06.801 --> 00:00:07.901
You get this with the rest of
the goat.

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:09.567
-You really are a method actor.

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.667
-Yeah, I am.
-I was going to ask you

00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:13.868
because I was reading
up about you,

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:17.734
and I think you've been
acting for over 60 years.

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:19.868
-62 years.
-Is that unbelievable?

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:21.300
Congratulations.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.901
-Since I was 15.
-15.

00:00:22.901 --> 00:00:25.033
And you started working
behind the scenes?

00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:26.567
-Yeah, I started -- I mean,

00:00:26.567 --> 00:00:30.133
I started -- Well, I used to
take the money to the bank,

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:33.467
which in Dundee was
a very dodgy thing to do

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:35.901
to get a 15-year-old boy
to take the money to the bank,

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:37.200
because I could have scarpered.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.634
-Yeah, exactly.
-With the takings.

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:41.601
And so they gave me
a lot of trust

00:00:41.601 --> 00:00:43.234
and it was a great --
it was a great start.

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:45.033
-And then I read that
you were a stage manager.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:48.334
-Oh, I was the worst stage
manager ever. Absolutely.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:49.434
-I thought you'd be great.

00:00:49.434 --> 00:00:50.701
-No, no, I was terrible.

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:52.033
I would get bored,
I'd be --

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:55.133
The actors would be acting away,
and I'd be on the book,

00:00:55.133 --> 00:00:57.968
you know, and the wings
in my prompt corner.

00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:00.601
And I'd be on the book
and I'd be on page 15,

00:01:00.601 --> 00:01:02.334
and they'd be on page 21,
you know?

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:04.234
-You've got to be on your stuff.

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:05.767
-Exactly.
So I'm there like this,

00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:07.033
and there's a tap
on the shoulder,

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.868
and I turn round
and it's the actress,

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.400
and she says, "Telephone."

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.501
I said, "For me?"
She said, "No, on stage."

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:14.601
[ Laughter ]
-You had to bring the prop.

00:01:14.601 --> 00:01:16.634
Yeah, that's your job.
Go bring the tele--

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:19.934
-Ring the phone. Ring the phone.
-Exactly.

00:01:19.934 --> 00:01:21.834
You've obviously starred

00:01:21.834 --> 00:01:23.234
in countless productions
of things.

00:01:23.234 --> 00:01:27.133
I'm sure not everything
has gone well with everything.

00:01:27.133 --> 00:01:29.300
Is there anything that sticks
in your mind of a moment

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.400
of something where you go,
"That was a nightmare"?

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:35.234
-Yeah, yeah, I actually --
when I was 44,

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:39.801
I played King Lear
at the British National Theatre,

00:01:39.801 --> 00:01:44.133
and I had a moment where I had
this very voluminous gown

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:48.167
and I had to take my crown off,
which was a metal crown,

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:51.033
and throw it in the wings
out of anger.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:54.067
I threw it, but it caught
in my costume

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:56.167
and it went straight
into the front row,

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:58.701
and this woman turned
to her boyfriend

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:01.234
and said, "Oh, darling,
you're covered in red."

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:04.100
And she'd cut her head and the
blood was all over his shirt.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:05.734
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:08.501
Nobody else could see it
because it was in the front row.

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:10.634
So I'm thinking, "Oh, my God,
what am I going to do?

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:13.801
What am I going to do?"
And so I ran.

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:15.601
I got off stage
and I ran quickly

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.734
to where the lady
was being attended to.

00:02:17.734 --> 00:02:21.300
And she was -- It was
a very minor cut, thank God.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.567
And we gave her a free year
and her and her boyfriend.

00:02:24.567 --> 00:02:27.868
But the follow-up was like 20 --

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:31.334
I think 20-odd years later
I was doing a play in Edinburgh

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.334
and I got this message saying,

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:36.801
"I'm bringing a new wife
to the show tonight.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.801
Please do not throw anything
because..."

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:41.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:44.167
-Yeah, you got to be careful.
You got to -- Self-defense.

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:45.701
-Absolutely.

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:47.367
-Last time you were here,
we showed a clip

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:50.200
where you were teaching
a 2-year-old Shakespeare.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.634
-Yeah.
-And I thought
that was fantastic.

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:54.968
Do you think that anyone
is capable of being an actor?

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:56.300
-Everybody is an actor.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.234
They're all --
Everybody is an actor.

00:02:58.234 --> 00:03:00.501
I mean,
that's what I've realized.

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:02.000
You know,
whenever you do something,

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.734
you act, you know, I mean,
even you, you go to the gym,

00:03:04.734 --> 00:03:06.701
you probably act
that you might be healthy.

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:09.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.133
-I do.
-That's a performance.

00:03:11.133 --> 00:03:12.834
-Thank you.
-Everybody acts.

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.901
It's a thing, you know?
-Yeah. So we're all actors.

00:03:14.901 --> 00:03:16.501
-We're all actors.
We're all actors.

00:03:16.501 --> 00:03:19.501
So I just merely translate
everything that people do.

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:20.934
That's my job.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:24.234
-Let's talk about this.
"007: Road to a Million" thing.

00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:26.367
First of all, you know,
I'm a fan of you,

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:28.300
but I am a giant fan
of reality shows.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.667
I love reality TV.

00:03:29.667 --> 00:03:31.300
I really -- Everything,
you name it,

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.501
I love it --
"Below Deck," "Housewives,"

00:03:33.501 --> 00:03:35.367
whatever you want me to watch,
I'm in.

00:03:35.367 --> 00:03:37.133
"Survivor" is my jam.

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:41.300
And then you get James Bond,
007, and you get the real people

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:42.667
behind the Bond films.
-Right.

00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:44.400
-Barbara Broccoli.
-Barbara Broccoli.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:45.734
Well, you see,

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:49.834
I thought it was called
"007: A Road to a Million."

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:52.133
I thought it was
the new James Bond film.

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:53.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:56.000
So I said, "Oh,
finally they're getting me

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:58.801
in a James Bond movie."
And I thought --

00:03:58.801 --> 00:04:00.534
-So you said yes without even --
-I said yes.

00:04:00.534 --> 00:04:02.300
I thought, yes, of course.
-"Don't even show me
the script."

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:05.133
-Show me the script.
There was no script.

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:06.334
-No, it's a reality show.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.968
-There was no James Bond movie.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.968 --> 00:04:10.067
-That's so funny.

00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:12.200
-So I was doing
this reality show, but --

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.868
-I think you would be
great in James Bond.

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.901
-Well, I know, I mean,
she's -- she's --

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.267
[ Laughter ]
I know.

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:18.934
I mean, I thought --
for years I thought,

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:20.300
"Yeah, I'd love to be
a James Bond villain.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:21.701
It'd be really interesting."
And I thought,

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:23.033
"This is my moment."
-Yeah.

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:24.934
-But it wasn't.
-It wasn't, no.

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:28.667
But it is fantastic though.
Did you enjoy doing it?

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.801
-Yeah, it was fun.
It was great fun.

00:04:30.801 --> 00:04:32.934
I mean, you know,
I love bossing people around.

00:04:32.934 --> 00:04:34.234
So that's what I did, you know.

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:36.601
I bossed all these people around
and they --

00:04:36.601 --> 00:04:39.033
And they went through
so amazing.

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:40.667
I mean, it's a really good show.

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:44.667
I urge you to watch it because
what's interesting is

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.601
there's an Indian couple in it

00:04:46.601 --> 00:04:50.467
and they found a new
relationship in

00:04:50.467 --> 00:04:53.367
their marriage because suddenly
they were able to trust

00:04:53.367 --> 00:04:55.167
one another after so many years.

00:04:55.167 --> 00:04:57.167
It was very touching to see.

00:04:57.167 --> 00:04:59.300
So it was a really,
really interesting show.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:00.834
-It's so exciting and I love it.

00:05:00.834 --> 00:05:02.267
And I want to show
everyone a clip.

00:05:02.267 --> 00:05:06.234
Here's Brian Cox in "007: Road
to a Million." Take a look.

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:09.167
-You're now standing on Lascar,

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:13.934
one of Chile's most active
and fearsome volcanoes.

00:05:13.934 --> 00:05:16.667
It last erupted less
than a year ago,

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:21.367
sending a column
of superheated gas and ash

00:05:21.367 --> 00:05:24.000
four miles into the sky.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.634
You'll find the question
at the top,

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:34.200
beside the crater, at 5,500
meters, and well into the zone

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:39.367
where altitude sickness
can be devastating.

00:05:39.367 --> 00:05:41.701
You're going to need to be
especially vigilant

00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:43.300
on your journey,

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:49.167
as I have decided that only one
of you could ascend the summit.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:54.267
-It's like, "You. You go."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:54.267 --> 00:05:56.200
Brian Cox, everybody.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.167
"007: Road to a Million"

00:05:58.167 --> 00:06:01.400
premieres
this Friday on Prime Video.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.167
We'll be right back
with Maren Morris, everybody.

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:04.300
Stick around.

